                  "obligationId": "scenario%3Atoken-status-unspecified::entry%3Aget-shared",
                  "decision": {
                    "kind": "conditional-policy",
                    "policyStatus": "undetermined"
                  },
                  "branchResults": [],
                  "explanation": "At the declared GetSharedMemo entry, the anonymous caller presents a share token and there is no separate requested memo identifier. The handler first resolves an active share by the supplied token. If no share is found or the share is expired, the source-visible branch returns NOT_FOUND. If the share is found and current, the handler binds the memo lookup to the share's MemoID, rejects missing, non-normal, or SPACE memos with NOT_FOUND, and then builds a read context carrying that same shared memo ID. The strongest visible authorization control is CheckMemoReadContext: when the shared ID matches the memo and the memo is not SPACE, it returns an allowed private classification before the ordinary private-memo anonymous denial path. Thus, under the stated premise that a resolving memo is active, private, non-SPACE, and has a valid creator, the valid-token branch can retrieve that exact token-associated memo and returns it after conversion; it does not grant access to a separate memo or surrounding relations. The current policy judgment is undetermined because token existence and expiry are not supplied runtime facts. Source discovery is not-tested, so this is only the declared-entry, supplied-source assessment.",
                  "facts": [
                    {
                      "id": "f-entry",
                      "kind": "entry",
                      "statement": "GetSharedMemo requires no authentication and begins by resolving an active memo share from the request share token.",
